WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.580
In this populist moment, conservatives
should champion and renew their basic

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.509
values, principles, and priorities, and the
economic policies that flow from them.

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:16.440
These commitments advance a particular
vision of society in which free markets

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.850
reward individual initiative, public
policy advances opportunity, and energy

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.720
and dynamism characterize our economic
lives. It's a society that demands

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.980
personal responsibility, self-reliance,
and self-discipline, but also recognizes

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.579
human imperfection and uncertainty, and
therefore allows no one to fall too far.

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:36.660
And it's a society in which mediating
institutions, most especially the family,

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.170
are strong and vibrant. Specifically,
conservatives should not retreat from

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:43.829
their long-held policy views on the
importance of economic growth, free trade,

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:47.789
entitlement reform, and friendliness to
immigrants. But conservatives should also

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:52.199
update their agenda to address low rates
of workforce participation, sluggish wage

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:56.190
growth, a health care sector in need of
reform, failing schools, and much more.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.219
Conservatives should remember that
limited, energetic government has a

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:02.850
positive role to play in a properly
ordered society, empowering individuals

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.100
to earn their own success, to realize
their potential, and lead lives of dignity.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.360
How do you think economic
policy should respond to populism? Let us

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:15.090
know in your comments. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:19.560
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.119
research and videos from AEI.

